---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Init Source Ltd - Terms of Business Summary"
  description="A transparency summary of Init Source Ltd's recruitment terms for clients, including fees, introductions, guarantees, confidentiality, data protection, and liability."
  canonical="https://initsource.co.uk/terms"
>
  <section id="terms" class="section bg-white">
    <div class="container maxw py-16 md:py-20 prose prose-neutral">
      <h1 class="h1 font-extrabold text-text">Init Source Ltd - Terms of Business Summary</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: October 2025</p>

      <p>
        This summary is provided for transparency only. It is not a legally binding
        contract and does not replace the full Terms of Business issued by Init Source Ltd
        before any client engagement.
      </p>
      <p>
        The full Terms of Business, once issued and agreed, form the legally binding agreement
        between Init Source Ltd and the Client. If there is any conflict between this summary
        and the full Terms of Business, the full Terms of Business will prevail.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Our Role</h2>
      <p>
        Init Source Ltd is a UK-registered recruitment company specialising exclusively in
        permanent Platform Engineering, SRE, DevOps, Cloud Infrastructure, and related
        technical recruitment.
      </p>
      <p>
        We act primarily as an Employment Agency for permanent recruitment and, where applicable,
        as an Employment Business.
      </p>
      <p>
        We operate in accordance with the Conduct of Employment Agencies and Employment Businesses
        Regulations 2003.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Fees</h2>
      <p>
        Permanent placement fees are calculated as a percentage of the Candidate's first-year
        total remuneration, including base salary and any guaranteed bonuses, allowances, or
        guaranteed payments where applicable.
      </p>
      <p>Indicative fee structure:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>18%</strong> - standard permanent DevOps, SRE, Platform Engineering, and Cloud Infrastructure hires</li>
        <li><strong>20%</strong> - retained, exclusive, urgent, senior, or priority search arrangements</li>
        <li><strong>15%</strong> - agreed volume, introductory, or partnership terms confirmed in writing</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Unless otherwise agreed in writing:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Invoices are raised when the Candidate starts employment</li>
        <li>Invoices are payable within 14 days of the Candidate's confirmed start date</li>
        <li>All fees are exclusive of VAT, where applicable</li>
        <li>The applicable fee percentage will be confirmed in writing before candidate representation or client engagement begins</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Retained and exclusive search arrangements are available and are governed by a separate
        written agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Introduction & Re-Engagement</h2>
      <p>
        A Candidate is considered introduced where Init Source Ltd provides the Candidate's name,
        CV, profile, details, or otherwise brings the Candidate to the Client's attention in
        connection with employment, engagement, or recruitment.
      </p>
      <p>
        All Candidates introduced by Init Source Ltd remain our introduction for 12 months from
        the date of first submission or introduction.
      </p>
      <p>
        If the Client hires, employs, engages, contracts, or otherwise retains an introduced
        Candidate within that period, whether for the original role or any other position, a
        placement fee may become payable under the full Terms of Business.
      </p>
      <p>
        This applies where the Candidate is engaged by the Client, an associated company, a
        related business, or a connected third party following the introduction.
      </p>
      <p>
        If a Candidate was previously known to the Client, the Client must notify Init Source Ltd
        in writing within 48 hours of receiving the Candidate's details and provide reasonable
        evidence of prior direct contact or an active recruitment process.
      </p>
      <p>
        Failure to notify Init Source Ltd within this period may be treated as acceptance of the
        introduction, subject to the full Terms of Business.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        If a placed Candidate leaves within 12 weeks of their start date, or 8 weeks for
        entry-level or otherwise agreed reduced-fee roles, and the invoice has been paid in full
        and on time, Init Source Ltd will provide a free replacement search for the same role as
        the default remedy, subject to the full Terms of Business.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any refund, credit, or alternative remedy is subject to the full Terms of Business agreed
        with the Client.
      </p>
      <p>The guarantee does not apply where the Candidate's departure results from:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Redundancy, restructuring, headcount freeze, or role cancellation</li>
        <li>Material changes to the role, salary, location, working pattern, reporting line, or responsibilities</li>
        <li>Misconduct by the Client or unsuitable working conditions</li>
        <li>Discrimination, harassment, unlawful treatment, or unsafe working environment</li>
        <li>Failure to provide proper onboarding, management, support, tools, or training</li>
        <li>Candidate dismissal for reasons unrelated to suitability for the original role</li>
        <li>The Client's breach of the full Terms of Business</li>
        <li>Non-payment, late payment, disputed payment, or partial payment of the invoice</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Client Responsibilities</h2>
      <p>The Client agrees to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide accurate and complete information regarding the role, salary, team, company, interview process, and hiring requirements</li>
        <li>Confirm salary, offer details, start dates, and Candidate acceptance in writing</li>
        <li>Provide timely feedback on submitted CVs, ordinarily within 5 working days</li>
        <li>Notify Init Source Ltd promptly of interviews, offers, acceptances, start dates, withdrawals, rejections, and Candidate departures</li>
        <li>Conduct all required right-to-work, qualification, reference, suitability, background, and compliance checks before employment</li>
        <li>Maintain a lawful, safe, suitable, and non-discriminatory working environment</li>
        <li>Inform Init Source Ltd within 48 hours if a Candidate was previously known</li>
        <li>Keep Candidate information confidential and not share it with third parties without prior written permission</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Confidentiality</h2>
      <p>
        All Candidate information provided by Init Source Ltd is confidential and must only be used
        for the purpose of assessing the Candidate for a genuine role or opportunity.
      </p>
      <p>
        Candidate details must not be copied, forwarded, disclosed, stored, or shared with any
        third party, associated company, hiring manager outside the agreed process, or external
        organisation without Init Source Ltd's prior written consent.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where a Candidate is introduced to another party by the Client and is subsequently hired,
        employed, engaged, contracted, or otherwise retained, a placement fee may become payable
        under the full Terms of Business.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data Protection</h2>
      <p>
        Init Source Ltd processes personal data in accordance with the UK GDPR and the Data
        Protection Act 2018.
      </p>
      <p>
        Personal data is processed for recruitment, candidate representation, client hiring
        support, compliance, and related business purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Candidate data must be handled confidentially and used only for the purpose for which it
        was provided.
      </p>
      <p>
        Data-related enquiries should be directed to:
        <strong><a href="mailto:contact@initsource.co.uk">contact@initsource.co.uk</a></strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Please also refer to our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy & Recruitment Compliance Notice</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Init Source Ltd will exercise reasonable skill and care when introducing Candidates but
        does not guarantee Candidate performance, conduct, suitability, availability, continued
        employment, or long-term retention.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Client remains responsible for making the final hiring decision and for carrying out
        all required checks before employment or engagement.
      </p>
      <p>
        Subject to the full Terms of Business, Init Source Ltd's liability is limited to the fee
        paid for the relevant introduction.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing Law</h2>
      <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales.</p>
      <p>
        Both parties agree to attempt to resolve disputes in good faith within 30 days before
        pursuing formal legal action. Where appropriate, the parties may consider mediation before
        issuing proceedings.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Init Source Ltd</strong><br />
        Registered in England and Wales<br />
        Email: <strong><a href="mailto:contact@initsource.co.uk">contact@initsource.co.uk</a></strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
